    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Corbin Carroll** (73.82) headline the Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup, both benefiting from a favorable draw against Roupp. **Moniak** is our strongest play; he sees a massive +14% park bump and significant platoon advantage, while the high 85% SB opportunity against a slower delivery pitcher makes him our primary engine for the scarce SB category. **Brice Turang** (71.09) and **Seiya Suzuki** (69.18) also provide elite value; **Turang** exploits a high SP_xERA of 4.93, while **Suzuki** capitalizes on a strong +13% skill-based matchup despite a modest hold rating from the opposing bullpen.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved leaving **Isaac Paredes** (48.59) on the bench. While his dynamic platoon profile makes him a viable asset, he is anchored by a sub-par matchup against Ryan, whose 3.21 xERA suppresses his scoring potential relative to our starting infield core. We are prioritizing high-efficiency matchups to preserve our game caps. Risk mitigation is critical today: **Jose Caballero** faces the stiffest test against Skubal, whose 2.78 xERA forces a -19% SP skill penalty, though **Caballero** maintains a respectable 52.92 score thanks to a +13% platoon boost. Meanwhile, **Dalton Rushing** is currently our floor-risk play, burdened by a late-order spot and an unfavorable L/L platoon matchup against Springs, but he remains in the lineup for his positional scarcity.",
